Third-party components keep their own licenses, which apply to those
components only:

Go modules (full list with versions in go.mod / go.sum and client/go.mod /
client/go.sum):
  - modernc.org/sqlite, modernc.org/libc and related modernc.org modules (BSD-3-Clause)
  - golang.org/x/crypto, x/sys, x/term (BSD-3-Clause)
  - github.com/ledongthuc/pdf (BSD-3-Clause)
  - github.com/wailsapp/wails/v2, desktop app only (MIT)
  - fyne.io/systray, desktop app only (Apache-2.0)
  - github.com/fsnotify/fsnotify, desktop app only (BSD-3-Clause)
  - github.com/zalando/go-keyring, desktop app only (MIT)

JavaScript packages bundled into the web and desktop apps (full list in
ui/package-lock.json and client/frontend/package-lock.json):
  - Svelte runtime (MIT)
  - libsodium-wrappers-sumo / libsodium (ISC)
  - qrcode-generator (MIT)

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, via @fontsource):
  - JetBrains Mono, Silkscreen, VT323

The Docker images (Dockerfile and scripts/build-image-offline.sh) include the
CA certificate bundle (Mozilla Public License 2.0) and the IANA time zone
database (public domain).
